// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
//
// Centered menu: a title, an EditBox filter, a two-column TextListbox and two buttons (Select
// and Close). The script rebuilds the list while the filter is edited, shows the selected row
// and closes through the menu stack.
//
// How the layout is built (rules measured on a live client, see references/gui-layouts.md):
//  - The root is centered with halign and valign center_ref plus exact position 0 0. A
//    proportional position 0.5 0.5 would put its top-left corner at the screen centre. Inside
//    it everything is in layout units: 1 unit is 1 px at 1080 rows, H / 1080 px on a taller screen.
//  - A modal root gets priority 998 (999 at most) so it draws above other UI. Do not copy that
//    number to a root that holds an ItemPreviewWidget; item_preview.layout explains why.
//  - Children are ordered by priority among themselves. A PanelWidget shows its color only
//    with style rover_sim_colorable; with a color and no style it draws nothing.
//  - The listbox reads its columns from the property colums, the engine's own spelling, as
//    name;width pairs. AddItem fills column 0 of a new row, SetItem fills the other columns.
//  - A button's own text ignores the font and size of a TextWidget, so each caption is a child
//    TextWidget. style Empty paints nothing: the opaque Bg child is the button's look and
//    keeps it from flashing on hover. The children have ignorepointer 1 so the click reaches
//    the button, and inheritalpha 1 so they follow the button's alpha (the script dims Select
//    with SetAlpha while no row is selected).
//  - userID on a button lets one OnClick tell the buttons apart.
//
// Script companion (client side, for example 5_Mission/MyMod/MyModFilterMenu.c). The load path
// starts at the mod's own pbo prefix:
